      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To extract numbers from a string in Python, you can iterate through each character and check if it is a digit using `isdigit()`. Here's how to implement it:\n\n```python\ndef extract_numbers(s):\n    digits = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isdigit():\n            digits.append(char)\n    return ''.join(digits)\n\n# Example usage:\ninput_string = \"h3ll0!w0rld\"\nextracted_numbers = extract_numbers(input_string)\nprint(extracted_numbers)  # Output: '300'\n```\n\nThis function will correctly handle multi-digit numbers and various edge cases.",
